From: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Subject: [PATCH] libstdc++: call pthreads directly with uClibc-ng

uClibc-ng builds pthreads into libc and leaves libpthread empty, and has
no __pthread_key_create, which gthr-posix.h takes as the sign of a
threaded program because uClibc claims to be glibc 2.2: every program
was judged single-threaded.  Call pthreads directly, as with glibc 2.34
and later, from uClibc-ng 1.0.59, the release this was checked against.

Signed-off-by: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>

diff --git a/libstdc++-v3/config/os/uclibc/os_defines.h b/libstdc++-v3/config/os/uclibc/os_defines.h
--- a/libstdc++-v3/config/os/uclibc/os_defines.h
+++ b/libstdc++-v3/config/os/uclibc/os_defines.h
@@ -38,4 +38,15 @@
 
 #include <features.h>
 
+// uClibc-ng builds pthreads into libc and leaves libpthread empty, and has
+// no __pthread_key_create, which gthr-posix.h would take as the sign of a
+// threaded program because uClibc claims to be glibc 2.2.  Call pthreads
+// directly, as for glibc 2.34 and later.  1.0.59 is the release this was
+// checked against.
+#if __UCLIBC_MAJOR__ > 1 \
+    || (__UCLIBC_MAJOR__ == 1 && (__UCLIBC_MINOR__ > 0 \
+				  || __UCLIBC_SUBLEVEL__ >= 59))
+# define _GLIBCXX_GTHREAD_USE_WEAK 0
+#endif
+
 #endif
